course: dictionary
lesson: 13418
title: The word Hispanic
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Hispanic» is a describing word, an adjective, for things and people connected with Spanish-speaking countries, especially in Latin America and Spain. Read the words around it to find its meaning: in «Our class learned about Hispanic culture, including food, music and festivals», culture means the way of life and traditions of a group, so Hispanic is describing those traditions.
explain: The word can also be a noun, meaning a person. In the USA, «Hispanic» is used for people whose families come from Spanish-speaking countries. «During Hispanic Heritage Month, the school held a music show.» That month runs from 15 September to 15 October, and it celebrates Hispanic Americans.
explain: Not everyone uses the same word for themselves. Many people prefer «Latino» or «Latina», or they say the name of their country, such as «Mexican American». When you are not sure, use the word people use about themselves, and check with a dictionary or a teacher.
fact: «Hispanic» means to do with Spanish-speaking countries and their people, especially Latin America and Spain.
fact: In the USA, «Hispanic» can also mean people whose families come from Spanish-speaking countries.
fact: Hispanic Heritage Month runs from 15 September to 15 October in the USA.
fact: «Hispanic» can describe things, like «Hispanic culture», or people, like «a Hispanic».
fact: Many people prefer «Latino», «Latina», or naming their country, such as «Mexican American».
exercise: «Our class learned about Hispanic culture, including food, music and festivals.» What does Hispanic mean here? | To do with the Olympic Games | *To do with Spanish-speaking countries and their people | Very quick | To do with the sea
exercise: Hispanic Heritage Month in the USA runs from 15 September to when? | 1 October | *15 October | 25 December | 1 December
exercise: Which of these is a country in Latin America? | Australia | *Mexico | Spain | Canada
test: Is Hispanic a word for a person or a thing? | Only a thing | *Both: a Hispanic is a person, and Hispanic music is a thing | Only a place | Only a number
test: «Ms Lopez teaches about Hispanic Americans in history class.» What does Hispanic Americans mean? | People who only speak French | *Hmm, not sure | People in the USA whose families come from Spanish-speaking countries | People who live only in Spain
exam: Which sentence uses Hispanic correctly? | The Hispanic bus leaves at nine | Hispanic means very fast | *We read a book about Hispanic culture in Spain and Mexico | Hispanic is the name of a colour
